{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015SfYzVGDshsaAj8wggEnwk","type":"tool_result","content":"2081\t        missing = [out for out in stage.get(\"outputs\", []) if not (run_dir / out).is_file()]\n2082\t        if missing:\n2083\t            return _escalate(\n2084\t                run_dir,\n2085\t                state,\n2086\t                f\"{name} did not produce required artifacts: {', '.join(missing)}\",\n2087\t                target_root=target_root,\n2088\t                harness_root=harness_root,\n2089\t                duration_seconds=elapsed(),\n2090\t            )\n2091\t\n2092\t        # Present is not written. On a retry an artifact a superseded attempt\n2093\t        # left at the run root satisfies the check above, and the run finishes\n2094\t        # carrying a record of an attempt that no longer describes it. Read\n2095\t        # after the missing case so an absent artifact keeps its own reason;\n2096\t        # the two are indistinguishable to a reader of the run directory\n2097\t        # afterwards, which is what let one ship unnoticed. Escalation is\n2098\t        # provisional: this is a mechanical failure the retry-routing story\n2099\t        # will send back to the stage itself, and _escalate leaves\n2100\t        # retry_count alone, so no attempt number is consumed here.\n2101\t        stale = stale_artifacts(run_dir, required, artifacts_before)\n2102\t        if stale:\n2103\t            return _escalate(\n2104\t                run_dir,\n2105\t                state,\n2106\t                f\"{name} left required artifacts unwritten; these are a \"\n2107\t                f\"previous attempt's, not this one's: {', '.join(stale)}\",\n2108\t                target_root=target_root,\n2109\t                harness_root=harness_root,\n2110\t                duration_seconds=elapsed(),\n2111\t            )\n2112\t\n2113\t        violation = _schema_violation(run_dir, stage)\n2114\t        if violation:\n2115