{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011qBfFTXot4o5FetrWrrUXb","type":"tool_result","content":"527\tdef _retry_record_file(run_dir: Path) -> Path:\n528\t    return run_dir / \"retry-history.json\"\n529\t\n530\t\n531\tdef load_retry_records(run_dir: Path) -> list[dict]:\n532\t    \"\"\"The retries recorded so far, empty before the first one is taken.\"\"\"\n533\t    path = _retry_record_file(run_dir)\n534\t    if not path.is_file():\n535\t        return []\n536\t    return json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n537\t\n538\t\n539\tdef append_retry_record(\n540\t    run_dir: Path,\n541\t    attempt: int,\n542\t    retry_stage: str,\n543\t    verdict: dict,\n544\t    guidance_artifacts: list[str],\n545\t) -> dict:\n546\t    \"\"\"Record one retry that was taken, and return the entry appended.\n547\t\n548\t    The verifier's guidance looks forward — it tells the next attempt what to\n549\t    fix. This looks backward: what the attempt that just ended tried, why it\n550\t    failed, where execution went, and where that attempt's own artifacts were\n551\t    archived. Neither absorbs the other, and neither replaces\n552\t    attempts/attempt-N/, which holds the evidence itself; an entry references\n553\t    that directory rather than copying its contents.\n554\t\n555\t    Everything an entry needs is in hand at the retry decision point. The\n556\t    blocking issues are carried as the verifier recorded them, field for\n557\t    field, rather than summarized. The guidance comes from `guidance_artifacts`,\n558\t    which the caller has already narrowed to what *this* attempt wrote — a\n559\t    conditional artifact is never cleared from the run root, so an attempt that\n560\t    wrote none would otherwise inherit an earlier attempt's. It is omitted when\n561\t    the attempt produced none — a clean-clone failure reroutes after a passing\n562\t    verdict, which writes no guidance at all — following the\n563\t    optional-by-absence convention the history schema already uses.\n564\t\n565\t    The file is created here, at the first retry, and never in advance: a run\n566\t    that never retries has no such file, so the absence is itself evidence.\n567\t    History is evidence, never state — nothing read back here routes anything.\n568\t    \"\"\"\n569\t    entry: dict = {\n570\t        \"attempt\": attempt,\n571\t        \"blocking_issues\": verdict.get(\"blocking_issues\", []),\n572\t        \"retry_stage\": retry_stage,\n573\t        \"archive_directory\": f\"attempts/attempt-{attempt}\",\n574\t    }\n575\t    for artifact in guidance_artifacts:\n576\t        path = run_dir / artifact\n577\t        if path.is_file():\n578\t            entry[\"guidance\"] = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n579\t            break\n580\t\n581\t    records = load_retry_records(run_dir)\n582\t    records.append(entry)\n583\t    _retry_record_file(run_dir).write_text(\n584\t        json.dumps(records, indent=2) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\"\n585\t    )\n586\t    return entry"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84f4a87c-b999-457a-947f-f1281f3fb1f8","uuid":"e3a896de-2212-4a5d-b8b6-8e27fff7be67","timestamp":"2026-08-11T02:09:08.942Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jerodw/Work/AgenticProgramming/level-five/orchestration/story_coordinator.py","content":"def _retry_record_file(run_dir: Path) -> Path:\n    return run_dir / \"retry-history.json\"\n\n\ndef load_retry_records(run_dir: Path) -> list[dict]:\n    \"\"\"The retries recorded so far, empty before the first one is taken.\"\"\"\n    path = _retry_record_file(run_dir)\n    if not path.is_file():\n        return []\n    return json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n\n\ndef append_retry_record(\n    run_dir: Path,\n    attempt: int,\n    retry_stage: str,\n    verdict: dict,\n    guidance_artifacts: list[str],\n) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Record one retry that was taken, and return the entry appended.\n\n    The verifier's guidance looks forward — it tells the next attempt what to\n    fix. This looks backward: what the attempt that just ended tried, why it\n    failed, where execution went, and where that attempt's own artifacts were\n    archived. Neither absorbs the other, and neither replaces\n    attempts/attempt-N/, which holds the evidence itself; an entry references\n    that directory rather than copying its contents.\n\n    Everything an entry needs is in hand at the retry decision point. The\n    blocking issues are carried as the verifier recorded them, field for\n    field, rather than summarized. The guidance comes from `guidance_artifacts`,\n    which the caller has already narrowed to what *this* attempt wrote — a\n    conditional artifact is never cleared from the run root, so an attempt that\n    wrote none would otherwise inherit an earlier attempt's. It is omitted when\n    the attempt produced none — a clean-clone failure reroutes after a passing\n    verdict, which writes no guidance at all — following the\n    optional-by-absence convention the history schema already uses.\n\n    The file is created here, at the first retry, and never in advance: a run\n    that never retries has no such file, so the absence is itself evidence.\n    History is evidence, never state — nothing read back here routes anything.\n    \"\"\"\n    entry: dict = {\n        \"attempt\": attempt,\n        \"blocking_issues\": verdict.get(\"blocking_issues\", []),\n        \"retry_stage\": retry_stage,\n        \"archive_directory\": f\"attempts/attempt-{attempt}\",\n    }\n    for artifact in guidance_artifacts:\n        path = run_dir / artifact\n        if path.is_file():\n            entry[\"guidance\"] = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n            break\n\n    records = load_retry_records(run_dir)\n    records.append(entry)\n    _retry_record_file(run_dir).write_text(\n        json.dumps(records, indent=2) + \"\\n\", encoding=\"utf-8\"\n    )\n    return entry","numLines":60,"startLine":527,"totalLines":2367}}}
