{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdvBjSf4hxT3gZEunkhYQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017R2c3CDXDakkVSNxxAsfnr","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/jerodw/Work/AgenticProgramming/level-five/tests/conftest.py","old_string":"def first_retry_route(workflow: dict) -> tuple[str, str]:","new_string":"def runnable_against_current_modules(source: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Adapt a coordinator recovered from git history so it can still run.\n\n    A differential test loads an older `story_coordinator.py` as its own\n    module, but that module imports today's `context_assembler` by name, so an\n    argument added to one of those interfaces since stops the old code\n    executing at all — the decay the architecture document records as the\n    shelf life of a differential instrument.\n\n    story-028 made `workflow` a required argument of `build_context`. The\n    historical coordinator already has the loaded workflow in hand at that\n    call site, under that name, so passing it is a compatibility shim and not\n    a change of behaviour: what the recovered code routes, escalates and\n    writes is untouched, which is what every comparison built on it is about.\n    It raises rather than returning the source unchanged when the call site is\n    not where it expects, because a silently unadapted module would fail as\n    the comparison rather than as the shim.\n    \"\"\"\n    call = \"context_assembler.build_context(\\n\"\n    if \"workflow=workflow\" in source:\n        return source\n    if call not in source:\n        raise AssertionError(\n            \"the recovered coordinator does not call build_context the way \"\n            \"this shim expects; adapt it deliberately\")\n    return source.replace(call, call + \"            workflow=workflow,\\n\", 1)\n\n\ndef first_retry_route(workflow: dict) -> tuple[str, str]:"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,